[{:db/id "q-97186/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "8115b771-4e3e-54fc-b500-fee828c7e802" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97186/selection/c6a9189afe903fc860b7e815f4b9c1b5df5b347da6d7c017799efa2808c74eba" :answer/id #uuid "71661365-fa53-5f69-8666-c63cfbc735ca" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97186/selection/f90dbdeb70230fe114ba47a0b645181704762024f2f7f1095364b83c08b414a1" :answer/id #uuid "287e35e0-fe90-52c7-bf4f-7ac56737b8c8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97186/selection/a61e54cbc4fe752895ee7d0648c2ab327d52d00df87e6cc86875833915075354" :answer/id #uuid "6aaacb3d-e06d-56ec-8f8f-9acc52471306" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-3-7\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97186/selection/71f893fe3e6205a25234d999b74bc7d00fb0973b3acd06d3074a7b14e4914301" :answer/id #uuid "b9d35b78-ec2b-5d53-94e5-6684eca0c7ff" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2-\\text{i}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97186/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "4817ab3d-9707-52d0-81de-039b292b0f9f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97186/selection/a61e54cbc4fe752895ee7d0648c2ab327d52d00df87e6cc86875833915075354" :answer-field/choices ["q-97186/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" "q-97186/selection/c6a9189afe903fc860b7e815f4b9c1b5df5b347da6d7c017799efa2808c74eba" "q-97186/selection/f90dbdeb70230fe114ba47a0b645181704762024f2f7f1095364b83c08b414a1" "q-97186/selection/a61e54cbc4fe752895ee7d0648c2ab327d52d00df87e6cc86875833915075354" "q-97186/selection/71f893fe3e6205a25234d999b74bc7d00fb0973b3acd06d3074a7b14e4914301"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97186" :question/id #uuid "88b94b51-b062-5eeb-8efa-fd6575e3a7d9" :question/math-academy-id "q-97186" :question/problem "Given that $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ is the standard Hermitian inner product over $C,$ find $⟨a,\\,(3+2\\text{i})b+c⟩$ if  \n\n$\\,$ $⟨b,a⟩=2\\text{i}\\,$ and $\\,⟨c,a⟩=1+\\text{i}.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties. \n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nFirst, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ is antilinear in the second argument:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,\\,(3+2\\text{i})b+c⟩ & =⟨a,(3+2\\text{i})b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =(\\overset{―}{3+2\\text{i}})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ \\\\  & =(3-2\\text{i})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we use the fact that the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-2\\text{i})⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩ & =(3-2\\text{i})\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute the values for $⟨b,a⟩$ and $⟨c,a⟩:$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(3-2\\text{i})\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}+\\overset{―}{⟨c,a⟩} & =(3-2\\text{i})\\cdot \\overset{―}{2\\text{i}}+\\overset{―}{1+\\text{i}} \\\\  & =(3-2\\text{i})\\cdot (-2\\text{i})+(1-\\text{i}) \\\\  & =-6\\text{i}+4{\\text{i}}^{2}+1-\\text{i} \\\\  & =-6\\text{i}+4(-1)+1-\\text{i} \\\\  & =-3-7\\text{i}\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-97186/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d59ac953-c511-5d6f-902d-4aeb804c99ce"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97186"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-97264/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" :answer/id #uuid "11261b75-1c15-5011-88c7-d1867147fb68" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97264/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "66b74a16-a25a-55a3-b76b-7a45689c8aec" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97264/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "d6a7b9bb-7fc4-545f-807f-9c546328ec61" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97264/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "01370c31-0294-5c8a-8239-6098e39882d9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97264/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "e7910e0e-f403-52a0-b630-fad878c73967" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-97264/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "747ac466-10cb-55a4-8118-04fb2e7ddb8d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-97264/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer-field/choices ["q-97264/selection/431472f1dab61ef54de031c09a96fb6a21dc69c8bc09f12797d1d686e8c9e8e6" "q-97264/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-97264/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-97264/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-97264/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-97264" :question/id #uuid "7bec15a8-acbd-5153-8a77-8304f45069a3" :question/math-academy-id "q-97264" :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C$\n- $⟨a,a⟩>0$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. Indeed, the inner product over $C$ has conjugate symmetry.\n\n- Statement II is true. By the antilinearity of a complex inner product in the second argument, we have \n\n$$\n⟨a,\\overset{―}{\\alpha }b⟩=\\overset{―}{(\\overset{―}{\\alpha })}⟨a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. Notice that if $a=0$ then $⟨a,a⟩=0.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-97264/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "42258cf7-c1cf-5cc3-876d-102cc2233083"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-97264"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-97305"] :question/problem "Consider the standard Hermitian inner product $⟨\\,\\cdot \\,,\\,\\cdot \\,⟩$ over $C.$ \nWhich of the following statements are true? \n\n- $⟨a,0⟩=0$ for any $a\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $2⟨a,b⟩=⟨a,-2b⟩$ for any  $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$\n- $⟨a,b⟩\\in R$ for any $a,b\\in {C}^{n}$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that the standard Hermitian inner product over $C$ satisfies the following properties:\n\n- It is linear in the first argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a+b,c⟩=⟨a,c⟩+⟨b,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨\\alpha a,b⟩=\\alpha ⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It is antilinear in the second argument. For any $a,b,c\\in {C}^{n}$ and any $\\alpha \\in C,$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b+c⟩=⟨a,b⟩+⟨a,c⟩\\,$ and $\\,⟨a,\\alpha b⟩=\\overset{―}{\\alpha }⟨a,b⟩.$\n\n- It has conjugate symmetry. For any $a,b\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,b⟩=\\overset{―}{⟨b,a⟩}.$\n\n- It is positive-definite. For any $a\\in {C}^{n},$ we have\n\n$\\,$ $⟨a,a⟩$ is a non-negative real number, and $⟨a,a⟩=0$ if and only if $a=0.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements. \n\n- Statement I is true. By the antilinearity in the second argument we have that  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,0⟩ & =⟨a,0\\cdot 0⟩=\\overset{―}{0}⟨a,0⟩=0⟨a,0⟩=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. By the antilinearity of a complex inner product in the second argument, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}⟨a,-2b⟩=\\overset{―}{(-2)}⟨a,b⟩=-2⟨a,b⟩\\ne 2⟨a,b⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false. The inner product over $C$ is a complex number, in general.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]}]
